+//
+// The pass supports direct OpTypeTensorARM graph interfaces and graph bodies
+// using TOSA.001000.1 or Arm.MotionEngine.100 extended instructions, plus
+// OpCompositeExtract for multi-output results. Graphs referenced by more than
+// one OpGraphEntryPointARM are not supported. Tensor shapes and attributes
+// needed to calculate output shapes must be ordinary static constants. The
+// pass validates requirements needed to calculate representable output shapes;
+// it does not replace dialect semantic validation.
+//
+// The request list does not need an entry for every graph interface. An input
+// request is required only when neither its interface variable nor an
+// already-shaped graph type supplies its shape. Output requests are optional
+// checks against inferred output shapes. Supplied entries must satisfy the
+// following requirements:
+// * No duplicate descriptor-set/binding pairs.
+// * Each shape is a full static tensor shape.
+// * Each shape contains at least one dimension.
+// * Each dimension is positive.
+// * Each dimension fits in a uint32_t tensor shape constant.
+// If provided, |output_shape_consumer| reports statically known, decorated
